{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"overall\": [\"C2\", \"C1\", \"C3\", \"C4\"],\n  \"keep\": [\"C4\", \"C2\", \"C1\", \"C3\"],\n  \"cover\": [\"C2\", \"C4\", \"C1\", \"C3\"],\n  \"lean\": [\"C1\", \"C3\", \"C2\", \"C4\"],\n  \"plain\": [\"C1\", \"C3\", \"C2\", \"C4\"],\n  \"why\": \"overall：C2最均衡，既保留v6的核心冲突，又补出了尚未缓过神的状态和熟悉感如何重新牵引他向前，比C4少拆步骤，比C1/C3多交代一层原因。keep：C4最完整地保留了不知道在等什么、也不知道往哪走，以及不甘现状、害怕投入失去、想停又逼自己撑住的双重拉扯；C2次之，C1/C3对不知道往哪走表达得较隐。cover：C2按照恍惚、硬撑又想停、熟悉感唤起向前冲动、舍不得重新出现的顺序，最能解释珠子中的感受；C4虽然更明确地对应了召唤和身体记忆，却把后段的身体牵引提前拆成了独立步骤。lean：C1/C3最紧凑，心理过程基本沿着不甘心、害怕失去、寻找理由、再次犹豫自然推进；C2提前点出舍不得什么并增加尚未缓过神这一层，C4则拆分过多。plain：C1/C3最像一个人在直接讲自己的处境，具体而不刻意解释；C2的认定事情本该如此稍显概念化，C4的有事等着回应、身体似乎先记得更像经过修饰的文学表达。C1与C3内容完全相同，因此两者在各项排序中并列，先后仅为列表排列。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "a55e64e5-1366-46d5-81f5-d8be3246a31e", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261030T004546753484Z", "elapsed_seconds": 87.688, "completed_utc": "2026-10-30T00:47:14.442974+00:00", "model": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "37c1fe4b1866021be220658043c87f522924bbf321f4528571aebc319dd1f0b7", "attachment_count": 0}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "yi/local-codex-auth", "account_sha256": "b3efb6361563c139233ed7b7ef61a7c9afe0bd48d4eb3525dbe31956b024d6da", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "atta